# Competency question: which business capability does an observed repository deliver,
# who answers for it, and what outcome does it serve?
#
# The question the two layers exist together to answer, and the only one that has to
# walk the edge between them. Somebody holding a repository - or a context pack about
# one - wants to know what the organization would lose if it went away, and that answer
# is not in the repository: it is in L1, reached through the one upward edge a person
# authored under review.
#
# Nothing here reads an observation instant or a commit. The repository path is an
# attribute a rename rewrites, and everything past tech:realizes is curated business
# truth with no expiry date, so this answer moves when the organization changes its
# mind and not when the source drifts. That is the whole point of the edge pointing
# upward: a capability outlives the system that delivered it.

PREFIX biz:  <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/biz#>
PREFIX tech: <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

SELECT ?repository ?path ?capability ?capabilityLabel ?owner ?goal
WHERE {
    ?repository a tech:Repository ;
                tech:repositoryPath ?path ;
                tech:realizes ?capability .
    ?capability a biz:Capability ;
                rdfs:label ?capabilityLabel ;
                biz:ownedBy ?owner ;
                biz:supports ?goal .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?capability owl:deprecated true }
}
ORDER BY ?repository ?capability
